# Rollback point for the PAT-1 window-registration change

PURPOSE
    This file records the last commit before a breaking change, and the
    exact steps to undo that change. Delete this file once the change
    has held in production for a release.

LAST GOOD COMMIT
    d159255  docs(debt-ts-1): do not nudge the apps team
    2026-10-21, CI green, tree clean.

    A branch points at it, so the commit cannot be lost to a garbage
    collection and nobody has to remember the hash:

        rollback/before-pat-1-fix-20261021-194530-d159255

    The branch is pushed. `git checkout` it to read the old tree, or
    use it as the target in step 4 below.

WHAT CHANGES AFTER THIS POINT
    88 component classes stop being registered on `window`. Before the
    change a consumer could write `new window.SizesPicker(options)` and
    receive an object whose 14 private fields are ordinary properties,
    because TypeScript removes the `private` keyword at compile time.
    After the change the only way in is the factory, for example
    `window.createSizesPicker(options)`.

    Every `window.create*` factory is UNCHANGED. Nothing that calls a
    factory is affected. Only direct construction breaks.

    Three static methods moved to plain functions at the same time:
    `configureCommandPalette`, `getCommandPalette` and
    `renderSmartTextTokens`. A reverted build restores the classes and
    leaves those three functions in place, so nothing that already
    moved to them breaks.

    Checked before the change by reading
    `component-library.d.ts`, which declares no class of ours. That is
    weaker evidence than a scan and was written down as though it were
    the same thing. **Scanned properly on 2026-10-22**, once the apps
    checkout was to hand: all 88 names, across `.ts`, `.js`, `.tsx` and
    `.html`, for `new X(`, `window.X`, `window["X"]` and `typeof X` —
    ZERO matches. The one name that looked like a hit, `ErrorDialog`,
    is their own component, and no page of theirs loads our
    `errordialog` bundle. Report filed at
    `~/Work/knobby/apps/specs/bugreports/2026-10-22-component-classes-off-window.md`.

    Four demo pages in this repository did construct classes, across 27
    sites, and they were changed to use their factories. Three studio
    demos were missed by that sweep and broke on the CDN; see the
    PAT-1 entry in CODEBASE_FIXES.md.

    One such consumer was found after the deploy. Three studio demo
    pages under demo/studio/ built their chrome with `new Sidebar(...)`
    and `new Toolbar(...)`, and the sweep above missed them because it
    read demo/*.html and demo/components/*.html only. They are fixed in

        ee406cb  fix(pat-1): three studio demos still called
                 new Sidebar and new Toolbar

    which also gave the sidebar factories an optional container and
    widened the demo gates. The knobby application itself was tested
    against the deployed CDN and works.

    Consumer-facing instructions live in
    docs/MIGRATION_WINDOW_CLASSES.md, linked from a banner on the
    documentation home page.

HOW TO ROLL BACK

    1. The commit that made the change is

           14e1298  fix(pat-1)!: 88 component classes come off window

    2. Revert it. This restores all 88 registrations and leaves every
       later commit in place, which is the safe option on a shared
       branch.

           git revert --no-edit 14e1298
           npm run build
           npm test
           git push

    3. If later commits have built on it, revert the range newest
       first.

           git revert --no-edit 14e1298^..<newest>

    4. Only if the branch is not shared and you want the tree exactly
       as it was:

           git reset --hard rollback/before-pat-1-fix-20261021-194530-d159255

       This discards every commit after d159255, including this file.
       Prefer step 2.

HOW LONG A ROLLBACK TAKES TO REACH A BROWSER
    Cloudflare Workers Builds deploys every push to main, so a revert
    reaches the origin as soon as that build finishes. `cdn/_headers`
    serves /components/* with `max-age=300, stale-while-revalidate=86400`,
    so a browser picks the reverted file up within about five minutes,
    and at most one request per client is served the stale copy first.
    A Cloudflare cache purge makes it immediate and is not required.

    `https://static.knobby.io/build.json` is `no-cache` and reports the
    commit that is live. Read it to confirm a deploy landed.

HOW TO TELL WHETHER THE ROLLBACK WORKED
    Load any component bundle and check for the class global:

        node -e 'global.window={};
          new Function(require("fs").readFileSync(
            "dist/components/sizespicker/sizespicker.js","utf8"))();
          console.log(Object.keys(window));'

    Before the change and after a rollback, the output contains both
    `SizesPicker` and `createSizesPicker`. After the change it contains
    only `createSizesPicker`.

